      <h1>How Bitcoin Core Releases Work</h1>
      <p class="msc-learn-page__deck">A Bitcoin Core release is the result of branch management, review, testing, release candidates, tagged source, reproducible-build work, checksums, and multiple attestations. Each artifact supplies limited evidence. A software release does not by itself activate consensus rules, prove source correctness, or require every user to upgrade.</p>
      <ul class="msc-learn-page-meta"><li>Bitcoin Core</li><li>Deep</li><li>Release Process Explainer</li><li>17 to 20 minutes</li><li>Reviewed 2026-07-25</li></ul>
